# Line endings are CONFORMANCE-CRITICAL here, not a style preference.
#
# `ruleset_hash` is the sha256 of the bytes of every .sch file and every code
# list a profile declares (apps/validator/src/validator/engine.py,
# compile_ruleset). architecture.md Part I §2.9 makes that hash the thing that
# makes a validation result reproducible and replayable.
#
# Without this file, git checks the same ruleset out as CRLF on Windows and LF
# on Linux, the two produce DIFFERENT ruleset hashes, and the corpus row written
# by a developer's machine cannot be reproduced by CI or by production. The
# specs.json drift test would catch it — after wasting an afternoon.
#
# Normalise everything to LF in the working tree, everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Conformance artefacts: never let a platform touch these.
*.sch     text eol=lf
*.xml     text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf

# The Makefile requires tabs; CRLF also breaks recipe parsing on some shells.
Makefile  text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf

# Generated contract artefacts — diffed byte-for-byte by scripts/contract-check.sh.
packages/contracts/validator.openapi.json text eol=lf
packages/contracts/validator.d.ts         text eol=lf

# Vendored third-party conformance artefacts — EXEMPT from normalisation.
#
# Must come after the *.sch rule above; last match wins.
#
# Everything above normalises OUR files to LF so the same ruleset hashes the
# same on every platform. These files are not ours. Their defensibility rests
# on being byte-for-byte what the standards body published: the EN 16931 and
# Peppol distributions ship CRLF, and `text eol=lf` would silently rewrite
# every line on commit. Then `ruleset_hash` would be the sha256 of a file we
# altered, an upstream diff would show every line changed, and the provenance
# claim in specs/PROVENANCE.md would be false.
#
# -text means git never converts in either direction, so the bytes are
# identical on every platform — determinism by not touching them, rather than
# determinism by rewriting them.
apps/validator/src/validator/specs/*/published/**  -text

# Binary
*.docx    binary
*.pdf     binary
*.png     binary
